    "BrochureContent": [
      {
        "ContentType": "Description",
        "SortOrder": 0,
        "Content": "\nPilot View Lodge is a distinctive detached home with an attractive slate roof, set within, yet separate from, Pilot View Apartments. Secluded behind electric gates with planted beds on either side, it benefits from a designated private parking space and is just a two-minute walk from Bullock Harbour.\n\nExtending to approximately 54 sq.m. (581 sq.ft.), this delightful home, with a side entrance and private off-street parking, enjoys a highly sought-after coastal setting that is sure to appeal to a wide range of buyers. Renovated approximately 20 years ago, it was transformed into a cosy and comfortable residence, ready for immediate occupation. It presents a wonderful opportunity for those seeking a home close to the sea in one of Dublin's most desirable locations.\n\nAn attractive exterior leads into a small hallway with a cloak cupboard, which leads into the main living area with a window overlooking the front. To the rear is a second room, currently used as a home office but equally suitable as a bedroom. Off the living room is a kitchenette with fitted units, worktops and a window overlooking the rear patio. To the right of the hall is the main bedroom, featuring four large fitted wardrobes and access to a spacious en-suite bathroom.\n\nOutside, the rear patio is enclosed by a high granite wall and quality fencing and is finished with paving slabs. This is an ideal space for al fresco dining during the summer months, while a garden shed provides additional storage. The property also benefits from access to, and use of, the landscaped communal gardens, which enjoy uninterrupted sea views, with social events regularly organised by residents.\n\nPilot View Lodge is a 1012-minute walk from Dalkey, Sandycove and Glasthule, where one can enjoy an abundance of amenities, including boutiques, shops, cafés, bars and restaurants. Scenic coastal walks can also be enjoyed along Coliemore Road and Vico Road, as well as in the beautiful surroundings of Killiney Hill. The DART is easily accessible in both Dalkey and Sandycove, while the N11 and M50 are also within convenient reach, along with several bus routes and the Aircoach. Excellent shopping and further facilities are available in nearby Dún Laoghaire, which is connected to Dundrum Town Centre by bus."
      },
      {
        "ContentType": "Accommodation",
        "SortOrder": 1,
        "Content": "\nEntrance Hall - 1.87m x 1.16m\nLaminate flooring. Double storage press.\n\nLiving Room - 4.78m x 4.32m\nLaminate flooring. Sash window to the front.Door to study / second bedroom.\n\nStudy - 2.98m x 2.75m\nLaminate flooring. Pitched roof. Fitted bookshelves. Door to the rear patio.\n\nKitchen - 2m x 1.78m\nFitted kitchen units with worktop area,tiled splashback and a stainless-steel sink.Appliances, including an electric oven and aHoover undercounter fridge-freezer.\n\nBedroom - 4.66m x 2.92m\nFour large fitted wardrobes and wall shelving.Carpet flooring and access to a large attic via aStira staircase. Door to the en-suite bathroom.\n\nBathroom - 1.86m x 1.68m\nWhite suite incorporating a generous-sized shower enclosure, wash hand basin in vanity unit with pull out drawers and illuminated wall mirror, pedestal w.c. and heated towel rail. Fully tiled walls and floor.OutsideThe property is accessed via electric gates with private parking just inside and neatly planted beds on either side of the doorway. The rear patio is enclosed by a high granite wall, quality fencing and finished with paving slabs and there is a garden shed for additional storage. There is also pedestrian access to Pilot View gardens which is very practical for day-to-day use.\n\n"
      },
      {
        "ContentType": "Features",
        "SortOrder": 3,
        "Content": "<ul><li> SPECIAL FEATURES</li><li> Distinctive one-bedroom detached residence, built in 1975 and upgraded c. 2005, extending to approximately 54 sq.m. (581 sq.ft.)</li><li> Set within, yet separate from, a beautiful and secure gated enclave</li><li> Enviable location, just 100 m from Bullock Harbour and a 1012-minute walk to Dalkey and the Forty Foot</li><li> New heating system installed in 2020, including radiators throughout and a gas combi boiler</li><li> Upgraded bathroom</li><li> Alarm system</li><li> Attic runs the full length of the house and could potentially be developed, subject to planning permission</li><li> Excellent transport links, with the DART, bus services and Aircoach all close by</li><li> Ideal for a downsizer, single person, couple or as a seaside retreat</li><li> Wonderful, easy access to coastal routes</ul>"
      },
